/**
 * Adwa Cyber — VAPT Center demo seed (NBE/NCB/S/02/2026/27 LOT4 tender).
 *
 * Rich bank demo:
 *  - ~38 assets across the pilot organizations (perimeter firewalls, core
 *    switches, DC servers, legacy Windows, Active Directory, Oracle/MSSQL/
 *    MongoDB/PostgreSQL, web apps, API gateways, vSphere, Harbor, Kubernetes,
 *    branch endpoints, one shadow-IT discovery) — the tender's §EASM registry.
 *    CBE carries the platform itself (http://localhost:3000) as a WEBAPP
 *    asset so the REAL DAST engine can be exercised live end to end.
 *  - ~120 vulnerabilities generated by the same engine that serves the API
 *    (buildSimulatedFindings + prioritise — one source of truth, never a
 *    divergent copy), plus curated KEV headliners (Log4Shell, Zerologon,
 *    PAN-OS, ProxyLogon, EternalBlue) on named assets so the story is
 *    instantly readable. Status mix: open / in_progress / remediated
 *    (on-time + late) / risk-accepted, with a few overdue criticals.
 *  - 2 completed scan runs per pilot org with honest engine labels.
 *  - 4 CBE critical vulnerabilities PROMOTED into the Findings module as
 *    NBE-22 corrective actions — proving the SLA/banner integration.
 *
 * Idempotent — clears prior VAPT seed data (and its Findings mirrors) first.
 * Usage: bun scripts/seed-vapt.ts
 */
